# File spec for ./validate.rhai — the module the Rust lane of
# /agent/src/package/validate.sdd resolves through its resolver dirs and
# evaluates as `import("validate") as validate; validate::run(args);`.
# Script semantics only: the clap surface, `args` injection, resolver-dir
# order and the `Rhai script error:`/exit-4 conversion are that spec's.
# Calibrated on ./../lib/secret_dockerconfigjson.sdd and ./build.sdd.

Spec: PackagesValidate

Platform: Rhai script (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine / locked rhai)

Purpose:
  Own the script side of `agent package validate`: read
  `args.source + "/package.yaml"` through @file_read/@yaml_decode, run the
  seven-throw manifest gate sequence over the decoded map, then re-read the
  SAME path through the strict @read_package_yaml model and run the
  @validate_options shape gate on the loaded @VynilPackage object. Success is
  silent — the verdict channel is throw/raise versus completion, and all
  user-facing text and exit codes belong to the Rust lane.
  Complete file structure: two @fn definitions (@validate, @run) and nothing
  else — no imports, no top-level statements; importing the module evaluates
  zero effects.

Exposes:
  @run(args) — the module entry, the only fn the Rust snippet calls; answers
    the Rhai unit value (its last statement `valid.validate_options();` is
    semicolon-terminated) and the snippet discards it anyway.
  @validate(yaml) — the gate chain over the decoded manifest map, returning
    the map (bare trailing `yaml`, possibly requirements-rewritten); @run
    calls it as a @statement and drops that value. Internal by convention
    only — no test or importer calls it — though any importing or shadowing
    module can.
  Import contract: `import("validate") as validate` over the caller's three
    resolver dirs — a package-local `<source>/scripts/validate.rhai`
    replaces this module and every check below wholesale.

Accepts:
  @args — the JSON scope map injected by /agent/src/package/validate.sdd.
    The one key read is `source`, joined as `args.source+"/package.yaml"`
    (the concat itself is written twice, identical each pass; a trailing
    separator in the flag yields a doubled slash). `script_dir` is present
    in the map and never read here. A hand-built map without `source` dies
    in the `+` join itself — no addition operator is registered for the unit
    a missing map key yields — before @file_read is reached.
  @validate — one loosely typed value; nothing shape-checks it at entry, the
    first @keys call settles whether it behaves like a map.

Returns:
  @run — unit; completion is the only success signal, no @print or @log_*
    call exists anywhere in this file.
  @validate — the input map itself (Rhai maps are reference types, not
    copies), including any `requirements` default it wrote; invisible to the
    outcome because @run re-reads the file from disk afterwards.

Raises:
  Seven @throw statements, eleven texts, first hit wins in the fixed gate
    order — surfaced upstream inside the `Rhai script error:` lane:
      - `You should set your apiVersion`
      - `You should set your kind`
      - `No metadata defined in package.yaml`
      - `No metadata.name defined in package.yaml`,
        `No metadata.category defined in package.yaml`,
        `No metadata.type defined in package.yaml` (one template
        `No metadata.${key} defined in package.yaml` per key)
      - `metadata.name should be a string`,
        `metadata.category should be a string`,
        `metadata.type should be a string` (one template
        `metadata.${key} should be a string` per key)
      - `options should be a map.`
      - `requirements should be an array.`
  Engine raises that are NOT this file's @throws, same Rust lane: @file_read
    stdio/invalid-UTF-8 failure; @yaml_decode parse errors including the
    multi-document package.yaml text; `@keys` function-not-found once the
    decoded root or a present `metadata` value is not a map;
    @read_package_yaml's serde rejections (missing required
    `metadata.description`/`metadata.features`/`requirements`, the `type`
    enum, requirement tags) and @validate_options' `Json decoding error: …`
    (both frozen in /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd).

Handles:
  Absent `requirements` — assigns `[]` into the shared decoded map BEFORE
    @run re-reads the file, where serde demands the key on-disk; the default
    therefore rescues no manifest (Tasks records the dead-default finding).
  Present-but-empty `options:` / `requirements:` lines (YAML null decodes
    neither map nor array): the respective throw fires, so authors must
    omit the keys entirely to mean "none".
  Non-map root document (scalar-only YAML) or scalar/null `metadata:` —
    engine @keys failure, not one of this file's throws.
  Missing or unreadable manifest — @file_read raises at @run's first line,
    so no missing-manifest throw text exists here.

Must:
  Evaluate the gates in exactly this order, short-circuiting on the first
    failure: `apiVersion`, `kind`, `metadata`, then for each of `name`,
    `category`, `type` in that literal list order presence-then-stringness,
    then `options`, then `requirements`; any throw skips every later gate,
    the strict re-read included.
  Read the file from disk twice per @run: once as
    `@yaml_decode(@file_read(args.source+"/package.yaml"))` for the gate
    pass, then once through @read_package_yaml on the same path text — the
    strict model sees the bytes on disk, never the in-memory rewritten map.
  Express presence as `in yaml.keys()` / `in yaml.metadata.keys()` membership
    and types against the exact @type_of answers `"string"`, `"map"`,
    `"array"`; no @try/@catch exists in the file, so every failure
    propagates to the Rust lane unchanged.
  Keep the engine surface to @file_read and @yaml_decode (core registrars
    per /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd), @read_package_yaml and
    @validate_options (@package_rhai_register in
    /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd), plus native rhai @type_of/@keys, `in`,
    @throw and template strings — no k8s, http, oci, shell, no lib imports
    and no top-level effect at import time.

Must not:
  Compare or default `apiVersion`/`kind` values — the presence checks never
    look at what is there, and the strict lane stores both as unchecked
    @String, so no convention string is enforced on this path.
  Write anything: the requirements default stays in process memory, the
    source tree is untouched — unlike the build lane's @pck::validate pair,
    this lane never @file_writes a patched manifest back (./build.sdd
    @improve_package is the writer).

Depends on:
  /agent/src/package/validate.sdd — sole caller: resolver dirs, `args`
    injection, discard of the snippet result, and the error-text/exit-4
    conversion; this file decides nothing CLI-side.
  vynil-core `0.7.7` @file_read + @yaml_decode — text read and
    single-document YAML parse.
  @read_package_yaml + @validate_options (/common/src/vynilpackage.sdd) —
    the strict re-read and the options shape gate; effectively the real
    manifest authority, since the script gates pre-check a small subset of
    what serde then rejects.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — the @Script::new assembly whose registrations
    give this file its engine names.

References:
  ./../lib/package_yaml.rhai (./../lib/package_yaml.sdd) — the forked twin:
    the build lane's @validate carries five identical throw texts but
    @log_warns-and-defaults apiVersion/kind where this file throws, and adds
    the `properties_improve` options rewrite absent here; cross-reference
    only — this module imports nothing.
  ./../lib/secret_dockerconfigjson.sdd, ./build.sdd — script-spec style
    calibration.

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the Scenario belows to tests: no test imports this module —
      @validate/@run have zero coverage (the `@update_package_yaml` tests
      around line 2000 of ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs exercise the lib lane,
      not this file) and no integration test drives `agent package validate`.
  [?] Dead default: `yaml.requirements = []` rewrites the shared in-memory
      map that @run then ignores, while the strict @read_package_yaml re-read
      lists `requirements` as required on-disk — a manifest lacking the key
      dies despite the lenient default. Decide whether the serde model gains
      a default or the script default goes (same finding reached from the
      Rust side, recorded in /agent/src/package/validate.sdd).
  [?] Weaker than the name promises, confirmed from this vantage: the
      `apiVersion`/`kind` gate is presence-only (null, `42`, a map — any
      value sails through) and the metadata gate is type-only (all three
      keys pass as `""`), with no convention, file-presence or structure
      rule anywhere on this path. Decide with /agent/src/package/validate.sdd
      and /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd which lane owns content checks.
  [?] Forked validator: a hand copy of ./../lib/package_yaml.rhai's
      @validate that diverged (throw versus warn-and-default on
      apiVersion/kind, no options improvement). Decide whether
      validate/build/any future lane should share one @validate.
  [?] Non-map inputs (scalar root, scalar `metadata:`, multi-document
      file) surface as raw engine @keys/@yaml_decode failures rather than
      one of this file's throw texts. Decide whether friendlier
      diagnostics get added.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a mapped passing test (script-level under
    ./../../tests/ or through the Rust lane), the `[?]` decisions are
    recorded, and `cargo test -p agent` with `specdd lint` and fmt stay
    green.

Scenario: first gate wins
  Given a package.yaml fully valid except for no `apiVersion` key
  When @run executes
  Then `You should set your apiVersion` throws and the metadata checks,
    @read_package_yaml and @validate_options never run

Scenario: metadata loop stops at first offender
  Given a decoded `metadata` of `#{name: "x", type: 42}` — `category`
    missing
  When @validate runs
  Then `No metadata.category defined in package.yaml` throws — `category`
    precedes `type` in the literal key list — and nothing ever mentions
    the 42

Scenario: strings pass however empty, other types throw
  Given metadata values `""` versus any of `12`, `true`, `()` or a map for
    the same keys
  Then the string set clears every gate; each non-string value throws
    `metadata.{key} should be a string`

Scenario: empty-valued options line is rejected, absence tolerated
  Given otherwise-valid manifests with a bare `options:` line (YAML null)
    vs. no `options` key at all
  Then the bare line throws `options should be a map.` while the absent key
    skips the gate entirely

Scenario: requirements-absent manifest passes the gate then dies at the model
  Given a package.yaml valid everywhere yet missing the `requirements` key
  When @run executes
  Then @validate assigns `[]` and returns, and @read_package_yaml raises the
    serde missing-field error — the default never reaches disk (Tasks)

Scenario: non-map manifests raise raw, not diagnostic
  Given `metadata: notamap` on an otherwise valid document
  Then the loop's first @keys call fails as a function-not-found engine
    error, not as any of this file's throw texts

Scenario: file trouble precedes every throw
  Given `<source>/package.yaml` missing, unreadable, non-UTF-8 or a YAML
    parse error (multi-document included)
  Then the run dies at @file_read/@yaml_decode before any gate text can fire

Example:
  default handoff: `args` `{"source":"/src","script_dir":"./agent/scripts"}`
    → manifest path `/src/package.yaml`, built twice by the `+` join;
    `--source ./pkg/` yields `./pkg//package.yaml`
  script-lane pass, strict-lane reject: `metadata` `{name: "", category: "",
    type: ""}` clears every gate, then @read_package_yaml demands
    `description`, `features` and a valid enum for `type`
